{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"c652c6bf27bb6c4677f7e80a26cb56d9e39f51ce95abbda82376baa02ed0ef48","digest":{"component_or_area":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh — secrets delivery to review-bot container","key_entities":["infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","infra/terraform/ssm.tf","infra/compose/.env","REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT","SECRETS_PATHS","BOT_PATHS","gerrit_reviewbot_tickets","/rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat"],"problem_keywords":["env delivery","autodeploy","secrets synchronization","SSM-backed environment variables","container deployment","review-bot","fetch-secrets"],"propositions":["autodeploy.sh rsync-excludes infra/compose/.env and never re-runs fetch-secrets.sh, so newly-added SSM-backed env keys do not reach the review-bot container on deploy without manual intervention","autodeploy.sh must guard the review-bot redeploy block on changed BOT_PATHS OR changed SECRETS_PATHS, and invoke fetch-secrets.sh before 'docker compose up' to pick up new or rotated SSM-backed environment variables","On fetch-secrets.sh failure, autodeploy must emit an err marker and abort the deploy fail-safe before tagging :prev or building, leaving the running bot on its current image and .env intact","fetch-secrets.sh is fail-fast and exits 1 without touching .env on any SSM error, preserving the half-updated-deploy-path safety guarantee","Code change is isolated to infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh (addition of SECRETS_PATHS trigger and pre-compose-up fetch-secrets invocation); infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh and infra/terraform/ssm.tf remain unchanged but trigger the redeploy condition"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825549584040571,"uuid":"82c7ce01-13b4-4110-85e3-c020893e4347"}